  "bio": {
    "eyebrow": "About Dr Lewis",
    "heading_lead": "Meet",
    "heading_warm": "Dr Lewis.",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Dr Alexander Lewis is an independent Consultant Specialist GP (ABN: 67 969 549 617) (MED0000941250) consulting at the Earlwood centre.",
      "Dr Alexander Lewis graduated from the University of New South Wales and completed his internship at Nepean Base Hospital and Repatriation Hospital Concord. For six months, he also worked at St Joseph's Hospital before travelling overseas to work as an Orthopaedic Resident at St Mary's Hospital in Kent, United Kingdom. Upon returning to Australia, Dr Lewis worked in a family group practice for five years before commencing his practice in the suburb of Earlwood in 1989. He is a Fellow of the Royal Australian College of General Practitioners, having completed the postgraduate exams set by the College. Dr Lewis holds Specialist registration with the Medical Board of Australia in the speciality of General Practice.",
      "Dr Lewis was a Board member of the Canterbury Division of General Practice. His interest in children's health prompted his appointment as the Immunisation Project Officer for the Division, developing strategies to improve immunisation rates throughout NSW and the Canterbury area.",
      "Dr Lewis is a former Medical Officer and Board Member for the Boxing Authority of NSW. His interest in boxing started at University. He was the Captain of the UNSW Boxing Team, representing the University at numerous competitions and becoming the Inter-varsity junior Middle Weight Boxing Champion in 1974. He has contributed articles related to medicine and boxing in Australian Boxing Magazines, some published overseas."
    ]
  },
